findings.body:
The diff removes `useRouter` from the `next/navigation` import and deletes `const router = useRouter();` from `BookerWebWrapperComponent`. The component still calls `router.push(...)` in four places (lines 193, 228, 232 and 238), so any of those branches now throws a `ReferenceError` at runtime. TypeScript will also reject the file, which means `yarn type-check:ci` fails.

The removal looks like an unused-import cleanup, but these calls are live. They run on the booking redirect paths, so booking pages that use this wrapper (team, dynamic-group, user and instant-meeting views) break.

::code{file="apps/web/modules/bookings/components/BookerWebWrapper.tsx" lines="190-200"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Restore `useRouter` in the `next/navigation` import and the `const router = useRouter();` declaration in `BookerWebWrapperComponent`. The `useRef` removal looks correct, since nothing in the file uses it.

::suggestion{file="apps/web/modules/bookings/components/BookerWebWrapper.tsx" lines="4-4"}
import { useSearchParams, usePathname, useRouter } from "next/navigation";

In the original `sortHosts` in `HostEditDialogs.tsx`, the equal-weight branch under `isRRWeightsEnabled` returns `priorityB - priorityA`. The moved version in `hostGroupUtils.ts` returns `priorityA - priorityB`. That reverses the priority order whenever two hosts have equal weight in weighted round-robin mode.

The non-weighted branch still uses `priorityB - priorityA`, so the two branches now sort in opposite priority directions. The function is called from `EventTeamAssignmentTab` (`handleWeightsChange` passes `true`), `useEventTypeForm`, and `HostEditDialogs`. Any event type with weights enabled will display and save hosts in the wrong priority order. The PR's human-review checklist asks for exactly this function to be verified, and no test covers it.

